-- title:
--   A normalized rough-head candidate lower bound
-- statement:
--   Let $W,n,K,h,u,v$ be natural numbers with $n,u,v>0$, and let $1<r_0<2$ with $u/v\le r_0$. Put $d=d_W$, $P$ equal to the rough-head modulus, and $g=d(2-r_0)$. Suppose
--   $$d\frac{Kh}{n}\le\frac g{16},\qquad \frac un(d+P)\le\frac g{16}.$$
--   Let $B=\mathrm{tangentBroadUpper}(n,K,h)$ and $M$ be the canonical rough-head candidate main term for these parameters. Then, with both quotients in the first inequality interpreted as natural division,
--   $$\lfloor n/v\rfloor\le\lfloor B/u\rfloor,\qquad \frac{3g}{4}\le\frac un M.$$
--
--   This turns control of moving-tail and floor losses into a positive candidate margin.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/ShouqiaoW/erdos/blob/61325b10bbdc29f4fb5e0618b414b9f2189333ad/390/lean/Erdos390/WholePaper/TangentPaperCleanListAbsorption.lean#L560-L731

